WEBVTT

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:18.970
Sister?

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.000
Oh, you mean that.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.120
I couldn't care less how that turned out.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.170
What?!

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:30.000
Rather, if it proved useful to our goals,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.630
that shallow existence served

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.340
some small purpose in having been born.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.520
Getting Miharu involved in this crap...

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.770
I won't forgive 'em!

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.510
What We Don't Know About the Real Setsu Chido
-Testimony from a Specialist
-What Does He Look Like?!
-Exclusive Footage!!

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.510
This Week's Ranking
A Major Slump?!
The Mysterious Masked Puzzle-maker Setsu Chido!!

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.110
Is the mysterious masked puzzle-maker Setsu Chido

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.530
in a major slump?

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.990
Things are amiss with the thrilling,

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.760
popular puzzle-maker Setsu Chido!

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.100
Even in popularity polls,
where he's held an unshakeable lead,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.250
he seems about to suddenly tumble from the spotlight.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.120
I swear!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.420
What is Galileo doing?

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.810
Lost

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.940
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.860
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.730
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:37.110
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.820
Found

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.040
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.540
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.330
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.460
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.800
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.680
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.390
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.760
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.970
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.350
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.810
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.520
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.360
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.190
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.360
It's now or never

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.450
That is what they say

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.530
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.200
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.370
That is what they say

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.540
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.040
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.250
That is what they say

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.670
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:42.890
Wandering Galileo

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.760
I did some looking,

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:52.100
but I couldn't find anything from that dome from before.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.150
They all just disappeared.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:58.990
It's like they never even existed.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:03.280
Once again, no clues at all about
the Orpheus Order, huh?

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:10.620
I, Ana, think those people seemed
like they knew Kaito.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.500
Have you met them before, Kaito?

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.000
No, I don't know 'em.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.520
I have no idea who they are.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.470
What they want is-

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.550
I don't give two turds about that!

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.220
If those guys will use whatever means,

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.290
I ain't gonna sit by idly.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.100
I'm gonna crush 'em!

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.150
End of story.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.740
Gammon...

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.200
Daimon, my boy, feast your eyes on this!

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.570
Mr. Naoki found a mistake in

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:47.080
a puzzle by that "genius" Setsu Chido!

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:49.870
You guys...

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:53.500
Try reading the mood, why don't you?

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.980
What're you talkin' about?

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:58.090
It's gotta be a printing error.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.050
This thing sucks.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.110
Is it really a Setsu Chido puzzle?!

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:07.130
It's a complete and utter failure.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:11.430
He didn't used to make puzzles like this.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:16.860
Um, who's this "Setsu Chido"?

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:19.830
A mysterious, masked puzzle-maker.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.030
He was super popular,

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:26.700
but maybe the rumors that he's all washed up are true.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.080
Ah! They're criticizing him on the Net too.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.030
There's a thread guessing how many days
till Setsu Chido retires.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.560
Setsu Chido's time is over, huh?

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.050
Still, I saw this coming.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.590
Well done, Nao-Nao-Naoki!

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.290
The good thing about his puzzles was

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:49.260
they had the pure emotion he'd poured into 'em.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.560
But the only things I feel from Setsu Chido now are...

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.370
endless anger, hatred.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.770
That's all.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:12.310
The Game has moved in earnest to a new phase.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:15.410
Is it safe to think that, Whist?

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.570
You are indeed correct.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:20.050
I would like you all to continue

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:24.420
to directly enjoy the Game with
Kaito Daimon and associates.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:26.300
That is the intention.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.570
"Continue to," huh?

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.040
Does something trouble you?

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:35.650
Kaito Daimon's who we're really after, right?

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.860
Why have we gotta go after those other chumps?

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.950
I know development of the replica Ring is going well,

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.330
but aren't we playing around too much?

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.700
Well, Whist?

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:55.120
You know nothing of this?

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.120
Correct.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.350
Fine, whatever.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:16.350
I'm grateful for your cooperation.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.260
Say, Doubt isn't here today, huh?

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:28.150
Strange for the guy who's so big on time to be late.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:32.550
I received word from Mr. Doubt
that he would be absent.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.980
It would seem that he's found it.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.150
A new toy, that is.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:49.050
I'm back.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:52.820
Oh, brother, welcome home.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:54.010
What's up, Miharu?

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:55.390
We have a guest?

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.290
Yes, one of your friends is here.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.890
Bastard!

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:11.530
What the hell are you doing here?!

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.510
Brother!

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.710
Let's go elsewhere.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:26.800
Bastard, just what are you after?

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.330
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.340
I'm not interested in your sister.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.930
She is no longer of value.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.500
Let's get right to it:

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.100
I have business with you.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:43.440
What?!

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.840
Gammon Sakanoue,

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.990
join us in guiding mankind toward a new future.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:51.150
Huh?

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:55.600
It would seem I underestimated you,

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.520
but I saw it in our previous game.

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:03.830
You have the capacity to work solely toward our ideals.

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:08.790
Man's true abilities were shunned by the gods,

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.300
and the doorway to true wisdom locked.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.120
To regain our full powers and return to paradise,

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.060
we must unlock that door.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.310
Via the power of the replica Ring.

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:24.650
That's why you involved my sister,

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:27.430
and Airi and the vice president...

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.950
Necessary sacrifices.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.150
Thanks to the data we received from them,

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:36.600
the replica Ring is approaching its full power.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.770
If the replica is completed,

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:45.710
even the vulgar masses not chosen
by a legitimate Ring

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.260
will be able to evolve to the next stage.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.610
Should you not guide mankind with us?

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.450
Gammon Sakanoue...

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.100
Come to the Orpheus Order!

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.880
You bastards.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.500
You're outta your damn minds!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.650
I await a more favorable reply.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:26.850
Orpheus Order...

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.410
Incoming Call
POG Entertainment

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.210
Hello?

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:45.960
Oh! Yes, construction of Tokyo Puzzle Land?

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.350
I'll transfer you to the supervisor.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.020
Urban Development Manager!

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:56.570
Oh, it's Gammon!

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.160
Been doing well?

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:01.390
Vigorously
&
Cheerfully

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.410
Whoa, things have really changed.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:06.830
The new POG must be loved by all.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:10.670
That is the policy of our new director.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.420
So, Gammon...

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.300
What can we do for you today?

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:20.680
I've got somethin' I could use a bit of your help on.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.970
It looks like you've got your reasons.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:24.520
What's this?

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:26.580
Can you tell us about it?

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:28.460
Yeah.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.990
Looks like you've had it rough, Mr. Chido.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:41.700
Antoinette?

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:44.540
You get it now, right?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.080
How tough the puzzle world is?

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:50.640
Still, a slump just takes time to-

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:52.040
I don't care about that!

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.960
I don't care about puzzles.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.490
There's somethin' I gotta do.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.840
Just get in.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:09.850
Oh...

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.420
So that's it.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:17.440
The POG is lookin' for the
Orpheus Order's hideout right now.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.030
What do you intend to do?

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.860
I'm gonna find where they are...

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.310
and smash their faces in!

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:29.080
These hands will beat the living hell out of them!

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.120
Till then, I can't rest!

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.470
Hey! What's that all about?

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:36.920
You think that will mean you've beat them?

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.170
Wasn't your policy to use puzzles to answer

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.050
a fight started with puzzles?

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:43.970
"Fight"?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.930
Don't talk foolishness.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.020
This is war!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.810
Who cares about puzzles?!

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:53.030
Do you really mean that?

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:58.570
There are people who will be sad
if you quit doing puzzles...

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:01.070
There's no way there are!

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.670
No one will.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:07.180
I only ever made puzzles for the money.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.700
I don't care a single friggin' bit about 'em.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:22.440
He really is dangerous, isn't he?

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:35.060
Hello? It's me, Erena Himekawa.

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:38.020
There's something I want to ask you.

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:39.220
A favor.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.050
Say, just what's going on?

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.450
I don't know.

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.720
It was like this when I got to school.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.300
I misjudged you, Gammon.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:10.470
Huh?

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.980
I never thought you were that kind of guy.

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:16.310
Bastard! What are you on about?

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:18.020
Don't act dumb!

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.520
This is...

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.280
your work, isn't it?!

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:24.820
Wh..What is that?

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:30.130
"To Kaito: Ron, ron, ron, moooron, mo, mo-"

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:31.770
It's Morse code.

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:35.310
"If you don't like it, make a better puzzle than me!"

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:36.830
That's what it says!

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:39.020
I don't know nothin' 'bout that!

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:40.330
It wasn't me!

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:41.710
Don't act dumb!

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:44.950
From
Gammon

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:44.970
Your name is right there, ain't it?!

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:50.030
He's right, it's written right there.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:52.200
I wouldn't write that, would I?!

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:56.100
Doing something that stupid is just like you.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.060
Hey!

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:00.270
You're lookin' down on me.
I get it, loud and clear.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:05.030
You think that, 'cuz I'm a Solver,
I can't make puzzles, right?

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.280
Huh?!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.160
This is a good chance.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.200
I accept your challenge!

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:12.300
Today, I'm a Giver!

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.700
Try solvin' my puzzles, dammit!

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.140
Okay, listen!

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:23.980
I've prepared three puzzles,

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:25.790
one each on the floors going up.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.220
If you solve them all

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:32.100
and reach me here on the roof, you win.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:35.020
Hey! That's the same situation

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.850
I presented you with way back when!

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.940
Dammit!

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:42.980
Well, that means you're birds of a feather, right?

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:43.770
Huh?

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.780
Antoinette!

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:47.950
What are you doin' here?

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:50.430
Wait, what the hell is goin' on?!

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:52.040
Now that things have come to this,

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:53.950
you're the only one who can solve it, right?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.950
What?!

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.040
Or could it be

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:00.960
that Mr. Chido Setsu the genius

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.130
is scared of losing to a novice Giver?

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:06.010
No friggin' way!

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:11.240
I'm gonna crush his dumb-ass puzzles
with these very hands!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:14.970
I don't really get it, but...

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.930
Good luck, Gammon!

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.410
Fight on! Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.060
Puzzle time...

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.610
You said it, let's begin!

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:33.320
Huh? "Use these 6 pieces to make the letter 'H'"?!

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.160
That bastard!

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:39.850
Use these 6 pieces
to make the letter "H"!

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:39.270
He just used the "T" I used that time
and made it an "H"!

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:42.240
Damn, pathetic!

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.880
I ain't got time to fool around with puzzles!

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:47.130
Done!

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:51.860
Use these 6 pieces
to make the letter "H"!

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:59.870
Connect the dots
using 6 continuous lines!

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:56.390
Huh?

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.100
He's rippin' off my puzzles again?!

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:02.430
I can do this in one sec...

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:08.860
This is...

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.900
It's the work of a novice Giver.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:15.910
A shockingly clumsy, straightforward puzzle.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.370
But...

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:20.310
It's not just a rip-off.

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.600
It's based on mine,

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:25.350
but he's added a ton of his own inventiveness.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.130
Not bad.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:38.370
Connect the dots
using 6 continuous lines!

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.640
What am I doin'?

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:45.510
I thought I didn't give a damn about puzzles.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:52.130
Solve the following equation.
What will "?" be?

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:56.270
What are they? Puzzles?

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:01.080
To me, this is...

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.130
Another dead end?!

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.050
I've had enough of this.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.480
It's gotta be a design flaw.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:21.930
This puzzle has no answer.

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.890
That can't be right.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.480
Even if we did solve this, we wouldn't

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.730
get a penny back for it, right?

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:31.940
I'm out.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:33.990
Do what you want.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.600
I'm gonna do it.

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:39.370
A puzzle as fun as this...

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.370
Money's got nothin' on it.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:45.500
Screw that.

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:49.500
You ain't gonna solve this puzzle!

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:51.550
It will be me!

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:02.260
So, that's it, I...

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:12.920
Solve the following equation.
What will "?" be?

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.400
Solved it!

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:15.940
This is a good puzzle.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:18.860
Oops! Not good!

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.380
Too bad, Gammon.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.540
You're ten seconds late.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.600
You didn't meet the time limit.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.640
No, I did make it.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.550
I made it.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.390
I was on the verge of

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:51.480
tossing somethin' I'd never get back into a ditch.

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:54.250
Gammon...

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.900
Kaito, I-

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:01.780
All right! Gotcha!

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.790
Wh..Wh..Wh..Whaaa?!

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:10.390
I haven't forgotten the grudge I've had since that time!

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:18.130
Bastard, you're bringin' that up again?!

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.800
Of course, dammit!

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:20.970
Are you a brat?

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.110
Anyone who says "brat" is a brat!

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:24.300
There's that same old comeback!

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.560
Honestly...
There's that same old comeback!

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.680
You really are bothersome, aren't you?
Whatever! You fell for it, Gammon!

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:37.280
It's me.

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.440
You know?!

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.240
Where is it?

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.110
The Orpheus Order's hideout?

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:02.480
Who it be?

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:03.720
It be special delivery.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:12.730
Sign here, please.

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:15.110
It's for you, Doubt.

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:16.910
Impossible.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:19.110
Mail wouldn't come for me here.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:22.770
It's from Gammon Sakanoue.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:26.540
How does he know where we are?

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:37.360
This is a puzzle!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:47.390
"Refusal."

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:49.140
He refuses...

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.740
He would say "No" to my invitation?

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:56.110
Your answer is only half right.

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:59.250
Try reading the next column, bottom to top.

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:07.230
"Foolish"?

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:08.950
He's calling you a moron.

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:12.940
It would seem that this time, in all ways,

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:14.890
he's beaten you.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.750
What is it, brother?

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:36.850
Nah, it's nothin'.

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:40.040
Anyway, Miharu, just you wait.

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:43.240
I'm gonna make even more interesting puzzles.

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:47.060
Awesome ones that'll make the puzzle fans go nuts.

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:49.240
Okay, brother!

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:10.390
He's gotten the POG to act, eh?

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:12.930
This is getting more and more interesting.

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:14.530
Mr. Freecell...

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:16.810
I know.

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:19.940
The new game is ready, yes?

00:22:20.430 --> 00:22:21.170
Sir.

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:23.530
Let's go...

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:26.880
to Root Gakuen.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.330
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:45.210
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:51.640
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:54.430
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:59.520
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:07.950
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:13.490
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:17.330
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:20.920
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:24.960
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.670
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:31.050
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:34.720
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:38.730
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:43.020
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:46.360
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:51.660
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:53.070
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:56.540
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:04.610
It's another team battle,

00:24:04.610 --> 00:24:07.130
and cute little me shall be your opponent!

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:08.630
Oh, wonderful, wonderful!

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:13.550
Cute little me shall bury you in the ground.

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:15.230
Yeah, yeah, wonderful, wonderful.

00:24:15.230 --> 00:24:16.960
Are you even listening?

00:24:16.960 --> 00:24:20.180
Next time, "The Decisive Battle is the Puzzle's Melody"

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:26.750
The Battle is Investigating the Puzzle

00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:23.480
I'm quite enough to deal with
a cute, younger character.

00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:26.440
Oh, my, who are you to call someone "younger"?
